From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:42:42 -0500
Subject: feat: move a folder to another Space

Tabs could go to another Space and a folder could not: Move to Space takes a tab
out of its folder, so a folder had to be rebuilt tab by tab in the Space it was
wanted in. A folder's header now has Move to Space, one row per other Space, and
a drop of the header on another Space's chip does the same. The folder goes
whole, nested folders included. A nested folder comes out of the folders around
it first, so none spans two Spaces. A folder of pins lands at the end of that
Space's pinned run; any other lands at the top of the rows under the line, its
tabs keeping what they are. The window follows it.

Why: folders F47, F48 (BACKLOG S-433). The owner asked for it on 2026-11-05.
Removable when: the sidebar's Spaces leave the series.
